    "problem": [
      {
        "text": "The 17 text-model overrides of prepare_inputs put the incoming token tensor in params[\"input_ids\"] even though they already passed it directly to prepare_for_attn and returned it as the initial forward state. Whole-parent-tree searches for the quoted key found writes, but no literal reads of that params entry.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_629ac04040da4fcb817090ac7c13acd0",
          "call_27cc19202ff34076b29cc6392f93344b",
          "call_adfe8b74410c46aaa22a10b990f5d89b",
          "call_87cb312dceca4cacb8d47ce1db6a8af4"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "reasoning": [
      {
        "text": "The deletion makes the explicit tensor argument the only input-ID channel used by the inspected text forward path. The old assignment stored another reference, not another tensor allocation. Removing it avoids retaining that reference through a caller-owned params dictionary; the tradeoff is that out-of-tree hooks can no longer rely on these overrides to populate or refresh the entry. The commit message describes the removal but gives no further rationale.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_629ac04040da4fcb817090ac7c13acd0",
          "call_60e991f0dac947768edb8afd5c42bd2e",
          "call_406ed35fe2844d8da5e7a4d613ab98a5"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "impact": [
      {
        "text": "Token IDs remain an argument to forward and prefill. A fresh params dictionary no longer gains an input_ids entry through the changed overrides, and an existing entry is left untouched rather than deleted or refreshed. This is not a global removal: the base Model.prepare_inputs still writes the entry, including when inherited by the Gemma3 and Mistral3 vision components, whose image-embedding methods pass image tensors through Model.forward.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_629ac04040da4fcb817090ac7c13acd0",
          "call_60e991f0dac947768edb8afd5c42bd2e",
