    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "forward-params",
        "title": "Pass token IDs as forward state, not duplicate metadata",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "The complete diff removes one assignment from each of Cohere, Cohere2, DeciLM, Dots1, ERNIE 4.5, ERNIE 4.5 MoE, EXAONE4, Gemma2, Gemma3, GLM4, Llama, Mistral3, Mixtral, Phi3, Qwen3, Qwen3 MoE and SmolLM3. Each still calls prepare_for_attn(input_ids, params) and returns its result.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_629ac04040da4fcb817090ac7c13acd0"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The direct in-tree callers found were Model.forward, Model.prefill and the research sampler sample_qkv in science/kv_quant_exp.py. Each uses the return value as x and passes the dictionary separately. Embedding.forward reads IDs from x, including when it selects indexed multimodal embeddings. The quoted input_ids in eval/model_diff.py names a saved tensor; the evaluation loop passes the IDs as module state, not as that dictionary key.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_a7f1381340d14f88914d3e4dd95faf60",
              "call_60e991f0dac947768edb8afd5c42bd2e",
              "call_0c524fe15c9e46e9b5b223f3c9507193",
              "call_406ed35fe2844d8da5e7a4d613ab98a5",
              "call_a2625be4ee084403aa6e724c6285b020"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Generation still supplies the token batch separately from its cache, block table, cache sequence lengths and indexed embeddings. prepare_for_attn still defaults to uncached FlashAttention; the uncached FlashAttention and SDPA preparation routes reject a supplied cache. Cached FlashAttention reads batch size from the tensor argument, accepts a supplied page table or builds one for a rectangular cache, and prepares position metadata. The rectangular sequence capacity must be divisible by PAGE_SIZE, 256 tokens per page. None of those checks or metadata writes depends on params[\"input_ids\"].",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_52edb1f72020429d9bbd55a263f67223",
              "call_50ac22feb5394cce87cc49944929dacf",
              "call_87cb312dceca4cacb8d47ce1db6a8af4",
              "call_8ae73e4291594d87a02342674854da95"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A standard-library check extracted all 17 parent overrides and the attention preparation helpers, then applied the one-statement deletion to each extracted override. Across 102 paired cases covering default uncached, explicit SDPA and already-paged FlashAttention preparation, the returned object and other metadata matched. The changed versions omitted the key when absent and preserved its old value when supplied; the extracted base method still wrote it.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_a403aa1befb945d9b6cf5082b1978b50",
              "call_629ac04040da4fcb817090ac7c13acd0",
              "call_87cb312dceca4cacb8d47ce1db6a8af4"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
